  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">PDO Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Revision of Procurement Legal Framework as Needed and Improvement to Pub Proc System</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2012-06-30" value="00000000" year="2012">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Procurement regulation partially revised as needed, No SBDs, No Public Procurement Manual available and Observatory portal unhelpful</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2012-06-30"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2015-01-30"></period-end>
     <target value="00000000">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Procurement regulation fully revised as needed SBDs, Best Practices Guides drafted and Observatory Portal fully developed</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="00000000">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">A new procurement decree (#2014-1039)was published in the Gazette on March 14, 2014 and went into effect on June 1st, 2014.Howeverthe Circular, SBDs and procurement Manual are not yet prepared.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">PDO Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Design a National Sustainable Capacity Bldg Program for Public Procurement</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2012-06-30" value="00000000" year="2012">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Unsatisfactory training program currently administrated by the Observatory</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2012-06-30"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2015-01-30"></period-end>
     <target value="00000000">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable Training and Capacity Building Program developed .</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="00000000">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Design of a National Sustainable Capacity Building Program for Public Procurement is still largely unsatisfactory and behindschedule, as the selection of the consultants to work on this assignment has been very cumbersome and too bureaucratic. Financialproposals for the capacity building component have been considered by HICOP to be substantially higher than the estimation and theremaining budget. As their first option, HICOP sought the possibility for AfDB to be a co-financier, but this solution ended upbeing not viable. As an alternative to re-inviting bids, the World Bank has advised HICOP to scale down the scope of this study andsign with the consultant a contract limited to the first phase of the service and aiming at designing the capacity buildingprogram. Regardless of this advice, HICOP has decided to reject all proposals,  revise the TORs and re-invite proposals.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
